/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 4.2 Bipolar Junction Transistors \(BJT\)) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Structure and Doping: Three regions: Emitter \(heavily doped to inject carriers\),) Tj
T*
(Base \(ultra-thin and lightly doped to minimize recombination\), and Collector) Tj
T*
(\(moderately doped, largest physical area for heat dissipation\).) Tj
T*
(* Active Mode Biasing: Emitter-Base Junction \(EBJ\) is forward-biased; Collector-Base) Tj
T*
(Junction \(CBJ\) is reverse-biased. Current relation: I_E = I_B + I_C.) Tj
T*
(* Common-Emitter \(CE\) Configuration: Most widely used amplifier configuration) Tj
T*
(offering high voltage gain and high current gain:) Tj
T*
(- Current Gain Beta \(h_fe\): Beta = I_C / I_B. Relation to alpha \(CB gain\): Beta =) Tj
T*
(alpha / \(1 - alpha\); alpha = Beta / \(Beta + 1\). Typical Beta = 50 - 300.) Tj
T*
(- Operating Regions: Active \(EBJ forward, CBJ reverse: linear amplifier\),) Tj
T*
(Saturation \(both forward: closed switch, V_CE,sat ~ 0.2V\), Cut-off \(both reverse:) Tj
T*
(open switch, I_C ~ 0\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
