(Solution Step 2: Calculate Collector Current I_C:) Tj
T*
(Assuming active mode: I_C = Beta * I_B = 100 * 24.04 microA = 2.404 mA.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Calculate Collector-Emitter Voltage V_CE:) Tj
T*
(KVL around collector-emitter loop: V_CC - I_C * R_C - V_CE = 0.) Tj
T*
(V_CE = V_CC - I_C * R_C = 12 - \(2.404 * 10^-3 * 2.2 * 10^3\) = 12 - 5.289 = 6.711 Volts.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Region Evaluation:) Tj
T*
(Since V_CE = 6.71 V > V_CE,sat \(0.2 V\) and CBJ is reverse-biased \(V_CB = V_CE - V_BE =) Tj
T*
(6.71 - 0.7 = 6.01 V > 0\), the transistor is operating strictly in the ACTIVE REGION.) Tj
T*
(Q-Point: \(V_CE, I_C\) = \(6.71 V, 2.40 mA\).) Tj
