T*
(* Q1: Contrast the V-I characteristics and underlying breakdown mechanisms of Zener) Tj
T*
(Breakdown vs. Avalanche Breakdown.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Zener breakdown occurs in heavily doped p-n junctions with very narrow depletion) Tj
T*
(regions \(<10 nm\). At low reverse voltages \(<5V\), the intense electric field \(>10^6 V/m\)) Tj
T*
(directly ruptures covalent bonds, pulling electrons from the valence band to the) Tj
T*
(conduction band \(quantum mechanical tunneling\). It exhibits a negative temperature) Tj
T*
(coefficient \(breakdown voltage decreases as temperature increases\). Avalanche breakdown) Tj
T*
(occurs in lightly doped junctions with wide depletion regions at higher reverse voltages) Tj
T*
(\(>6V\). Thermally generated minority carriers accelerate across the depletion field,) Tj
T*
(colliding with crystal lattice atoms and knocking out valence electrons \(impact) Tj
T*
(ionization\), triggering an exponential carrier avalanche. It exhibits a positive) Tj
T*
(temperature coefficient \(breakdown voltage increases with temperature due to increased) Tj
T*
(lattice vibrations scattering carriers\).) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Explain the input and output characteristics of a BJT in Common-Emitter \(CE\)) Tj
T*
(configuration, defining the Early Effect.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Input characteristics plot I_B vs. V_BE at constant V_CE, resembling a) Tj
T*
(forward-biased diode with cut-in voltage ~0.7V for silicon. Output characteristics plot) Tj
T*
(I_C vs. V_CE at constant I_B, showing three regions: Saturation \(V_CE < 0.2V, current) Tj
T*
(rises steeply\), Active \(nearly horizontal curves where I_C = Beta*I_B\), and Cut-off \(I_B) Tj
T*
(= 0, tiny leakage current\). The Early Effect \(Base-Width Modulation\) refers to the) Tj
T*
(narrowing of the effective metallurgical base width as reverse-bias collector voltage) Tj
T*
(V_CE increases. A narrower base reduces recombination, causing a slight upward tilt in) Tj
T*
(the active-region output characteristics. When extrapolated backward, all output) Tj
T*
(characteristic curves intersect at a single negative voltage on the V_CE axis termed the) Tj
T*
(Early Voltage \(V_A ~ 50-100V\).) Tj
